                                ELB
                        Elastic Load Balancer

--> Load balancer distributes the incoming web traffic among avaialble servers.
--> Features:
1. High avaialability
2. Fault tolerance

--> ELB types:
1. Application Load Balancer: (ALB)
--> HTTP and HTTPS traffic
--> Path based routing
--> Application LB works on 7th layer of OSI model which Application layer.

2. Network Load Balancer: (NLB)
--> TCP and UDP traffic 
--> ultra low latency
--> handle millions request per sec 
--> Network LB works on 4th layer of OSI model which is transport layer.

3. Gateway Load Balancer:
--> Security 

4. Claasic Load Balancer: Prev gen

Shell Script :
#!/bin/bash 
sudo su -
yum install httpd -y
systemctl start httpd 
systemctl enable httpd
echo "<h1>comment</h1>" >/var/www/html/index.html

**Listeners:
-->A Listener is a process that checks for incoming connection requests
 on a specific protocol and port.

**Target Group:
--> A Target Group is a collection of backend resources (targets) where the load balancer sends incoming requests.

Targets can include:
1. EC2 instances
2. IP addresses

